---
import GlasshouseLayout from '../../components/GlasshouseLayout.astro';
---

<GlasshouseLayout
  title="About — Glasshouse Systems Studio"
  description="The operator behind Glasshouse Systems Studio: twenty-five years of institutional-scale systems work, applied to small business."
  activePage="/work/about"
>
  <section class="stratum stratum--cream opener" aria-labelledby="about-h">
    <div class="opener-inner">
      <p class="gh-eyebrow">The Operator</p>
      <h1 id="about-h">One operator. Twenty‑five years of systems that had to work.</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stratum stratum--cream bio" aria-label="Biography">
    <div class="bio-inner">
      <figure class="bio-portrait">
        <img
          src="/about-portrait.png"
          alt="J. Burroughs — the operator, writing in a notebook"
          width="360"
          loading="eager"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <figcaption>
          <span class="bio-name">J. Burroughs</span>
          <span class="bio-role">Founder · Operator</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="bio-body">
        <p>
          Glasshouse Systems Studio is the working practice of J. Burroughs — a systems
          designer with twenty-five years inside healthcare supply chain at an academic
          medical center. High-stakes procurement, multi-vendor coordination, evidence-based
          analysis for surgeons and clinical staff, and the specific discipline of keeping
          systems functional under conditions they weren't designed for.
        </p>
        <p>
          That work produced a method. Understand how the work actually flows before touching
          any tools. Design for clarity. Automate second. Keep the human in the loop, always.
          Glasshouse applies that method to small and medium businesses — environments where
          the infrastructure has gotten ahead of the owner's ability to see it clearly.
        </p>
        <p>
          The studio runs its own multi-machine research and automation stack, and every
          system it offers a client has already earned its keep in daily production here.
          That standard doesn't bend: if it wouldn't survive real operations, it isn't sold.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stratum stratum--dark tenets" aria-labelledby="tenets-h">
    <div class="tenets-inner">
      <header class="tenets-opening">
        <p class="gh-eyebrow">How the Studio Thinks</p>
        <h2 id="tenets-h">Three tenets. Every engagement.</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="tenet-row">
        <article class="tenet">
          <p class="tenet-num" aria-hidden="true">I</p>
          <h3>Clarity before complexity</h3>
          <p>You should be able to understand your own systems — trace them, question them, and correct them without calling anyone.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="tenet">
          <p class="tenet-num" aria-hidden="true">II</p>
          <h3>Structure before tools</h3>
          <p>Tools change every season. The shape of your work is the asset — we design that first, then pick the tools that serve it.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="tenet">
          <p class="tenet-num" aria-hidden="true">III</p>
          <h3>Human in the loop</h3>
          <p>Nothing runs that you can't see and stop. Automation earns autonomy gradually — it is never granted on faith.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stratum stratum--cream studio" aria-labelledby="studio-h">
    <div class="studio-inner">
      <div class="studio-copy">
        <p class="gh-eyebrow">The Studio</p>
        <h2 id="studio-h">A small studio, on purpose.</h2>
        <p>
          Glasshouse is a studio of Lithium Dreams Industries, based in Iowa. It stays small
          so the person who designs your system is the person who builds it, documents it,
          and answers for it. No handoffs to a bench you never meet.
        </p>
        <a href="/work/intake/" class="btn-plaque">Start Your Brief</a>
      </div>
      <p class="studio-footnote">
        Lithium Dreams also maintains a roadside attraction at the edge of the universe.
        Visitors welcome. <a href="/attraction">The Attraction →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</GlasshouseLayout>

<style>
  .opener-inner {
    padding: clamp(3.5rem, 8vh, 6rem) 0 clamp(2rem, 4vh, 3rem);
  }
  .opener-inner h1 {
    font-family: var(--gh-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5.9vw, 7rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.08;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .bio-inner {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(240px, 360px) minmax(0, 58ch);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 5rem);
    align-items: start;
    padding-bottom: clamp(3.5rem, 8vh, 6rem);
  }
  .bio-portrait img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
    border: 1px solid var(--gh-brass-edge);
  }
  .bio-portrait figcaption {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.15rem;
    padding-top: 0.85rem;
  }
  .bio-name {
    font-family: var(--gh-display);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }
  .bio-role {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--gh-ink-soft);
  }
  .bio-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.4rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1rem + 0.2vw, 1.2rem);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .tenets-inner {
    padding: clamp(3.5rem, 8vh, 5.5rem) 0;
  }
  .tenets-opening h2 {
    font-family: var(--gh-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 2.4vw, 2.3rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    margin: 1rem 0 2.5rem;
  }
  .tenet-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 3rem);
  }
  .tenet {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--gh-hairline-light);
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
  }
  .tenet-num {
    font-family: var(--gh-display);
    color: var(--gh-brass-bright);
    font-size: 1rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  }
  .tenet h3 {
    font-family: var(--gh-serif);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 0.6rem 0 0.6rem;
  }
  .tenet p:last-child {
    font-size: 0.98rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--gh-cream-soft);
  }

  .studio-inner {
    padding: clamp(3.5rem, 8vh, 6rem) 0 clamp(2.5rem, 5vh, 4rem);
  }
  .studio-copy {
    max-width: 58ch;
  }
  .studio-copy h2 {
    font-family: var(--gh-serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 2.6vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    margin: 1rem 0 1.25rem;
  }
  .studio-copy p {
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1rem + 0.2vw, 1.2rem);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .studio-footnote {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--gh-hairline-dark);
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 6vh, 4.5rem);
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--gh-ink-soft);
  }
  .studio-footnote a {
    color: var(--gh-teal-ink);
    font-style: normal;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .studio-footnote a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .bio-inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .bio-portrait { max-width: 300px; }
    .tenet-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
